# AI-BOS Engineering OS Binding

When working in the Engineering OS lane, treat delivery context as **`PRJ-ENG-SAASOS-001`** (Engineering department, peer to Marketing OS).

## Mandatory

1. Read `AI-BOS/project-registry/registry.json` entry `PRJ-ENG-SAASOS-001`.
2. Load `RU-AI-BOS-ENGOS-001` + `HB-ENG-CTO-001` + division handbook.
3. Persist to `founder-os-memory/projects/<slug>/engineering/` per `TP-ENG-SAASOS-001`.
4. End with Bangla handoff per `RU-AI-BOS-HANDOFF-001`.

## Routing

| Need | Agent |
|------|-------|
| Engineering department / multi-track | `@engineering-cto` (`AG-ENG-CTO-001`) |
| Full-stack SaaS (web/) | `@senior-saas-developer` (via CTO brief) |
| HTML templates | `@frontend-architect` |
| Next.js migration | `@nextjs-migration-architect` |
| Performance / CWV | `@eng-performance` |
| Docs / ADRs / runbooks | `@eng-documentation` |
| Marketing coordination | `@marketing-cmo` |
| Business context | `@founder-os` |

## Human gates

Production deploy, secrets, OAuth, payments — stop with Bangla click-by-click instructions.

## Never

Skip phase-end quality enforcers; bypass CTO on cross-track engineering programs from Founder; auto-deploy to production.

Knowledge-layer mirror: `RU-AI-BOS-ENGOS-001`.
